WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.797 --> 00:00:16.500
The earl continued to shower Cedric with gifts.

2
00:00:18.341 --> 00:00:23.322
Another boy might become spoiled, but Cedric was still under his mother's influence.

3
00:00:24.903 --> 00:00:28.784
So he remained the same thoughtful, unselfish boy he'd always been.

4
00:00:30.408 --> 00:00:32.670
Cedric and the earl were becoming good friends.

5
00:00:35.853 --> 00:00:39.195
On sunny days the earl watched Cedric's riding lessons.

6
00:00:41.257 --> 00:00:45.160
On rainy days they stayed inside and played the baseball game together.

7
00:00:47.582 --> 00:00:50.225
One rainy day the earl's doctor came to visit.

8
00:00:51.806 --> 00:00:53.607
Cedric put away the baseball game.

9
00:00:55.008 --> 00:00:58.952
Then he played quietly with Dougal while the two men talked in the library.

10
00:01:00.536 --> 00:01:04.479
"You haven't mentioned your gout lately," the doctor said to the earl.

11
00:01:04.499 --> 00:01:07.841
"Is your foot bothering you?"

12
00:01:07.861 --> 00:01:11.984
"Now that you mention it The earl paused.

13
00:01:13.065 --> 00:01:15.186
"I haven't noticed the pain as much."

14
00:01:17.148 --> 00:01:20.250
"Perhaps that's because you have other things to think about."

15
00:01:21.571 --> 00:01:23.632
The doctor gestured toward Cedric.

16
00:01:23.652 --> 00:01:29.156
"Well, perhaps," the earl said in a gruff voice.

17
00:01:30.292 --> 00:01:33.074
The earl didn't like to admit to others that they were right.

18
00:01:34.275 --> 00:01:38.599
But he admitted to himself that time passed more quickly when Cedric was around.

19
00:01:40.781 --> 00:01:44.944
The next day was sunny, so Cedric and the earl went to the stables together.

20
00:01:44.964 --> 00:01:49.348
"I wish you'd go riding with me," Cedric said.

21
00:01:49.368 --> 00:01:52.530
"It would be such fun if you'd ride too."

22
00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:54.712
"Fun, you say?

23
00:01:54.732 --> 00:01:59.256
Hmm." For a moment the earl looked thoughtful.

24
00:02:00.748 --> 00:02:02.369
Then he summoned the head groom.

25
00:02:02.389 --> 00:02:05.511
"Wilkins, saddle my horse!

26
00:02:06.732 --> 00:02:09.654
I'm taking Lord Fauntleroy riding this morning."

27
00:02:09.674 --> 00:02:14.678
"But you haven't ridden in years," Wilkins said.

28
00:02:14.698 --> 00:02:17.219
"Are you sure, my lord?"

29
00:02:17.239 --> 00:02:19.921
"Don't just stand there!"

30
00:02:20.882 --> 00:02:23.323
The earl started to turn purple with rage.

31
00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:26.926
"Lord Fauntleroy and I are waiting!"

32
00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:31.477
"I just—I mean—yes, my lord!"

33
00:02:32.398 --> 00:02:35.440
Wilkins was flustered by the earl's unexpected order.

34
00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:39.063
"It'll only take a few minutes, my lord."

35
00:02:43.166 --> 00:02:46.689
After that the earl rode with his grandson almost every day.

36
00:02:48.610 --> 00:02:52.373
As they traveled along the country roads, Cedric chatted away.

37
00:02:53.634 --> 00:02:55.716
Much of the time, he talked about his mother.

38
00:02:56.896 --> 00:02:58.777
The earl soon learned that Mrs.

39
00:02:58.917 --> 00:03:00.117
Errol led a busy life.

40
00:03:00.137 --> 00:03:05.479
"Everyone knows her and loves her," Cedric said proudly.

41
00:03:05.499 --> 00:03:08.980
"It's a good thing my mother has her own carriage!

42
00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:12.441
She's always visiting anybody who needs help.

43
00:03:14.501 --> 00:03:18.622
She brings food to the poor and sits with the sick and the lonely.

44
00:03:19.663 --> 00:03:25.068
There are even some children who come to her house to learn to sew!"

45
00:03:25.088 --> 00:03:27.810
The earl didn't like to hear Cedric talk about his mother.

46
00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:30.952
But he was curious about one thing.

47
00:03:30.972 --> 00:03:36.475
"Why does your mother do so much for people she hardly knows?"

48
00:03:37.115 --> 00:03:37.775
he asked.

49
00:03:37.795 --> 00:03:40.337
"Oh, that's easy."

50
00:03:41.197 --> 00:03:43.319
Cedric smiled up at his grandfather.

51
00:03:43.339 --> 00:03:46.881
"We didn't have much money in New York.

52
00:03:47.741 --> 00:03:49.142
But now she feels rich!

53
00:03:50.143 --> 00:03:52.344
So she wants to help anyone she can."

54
00:03:56.396 --> 00:03:59.318
By this point the two riders had reached an overlook.

55
00:04:00.698 --> 00:04:04.941
From here they had a wide view of everything below and the castle in the distance.

56
00:04:06.241 --> 00:04:09.763
The earl made a sweeping gesture that took in the whole scene.

57
00:04:09.783 --> 00:04:14.946
"Do you know that all this land belongs to me?"

58
00:04:15.346 --> 00:04:16.467
he asked Cedric.

59
00:04:16.487 --> 00:04:20.849
"That's a lot of land to belong to one person!"

60
00:04:20.869 --> 00:04:25.392
"And one day it will all belong to you."

61
00:04:27.208 --> 00:04:28.469
Cedric was awestruck.

62
00:04:29.569 --> 00:04:32.230
In a quiet voice, he asked, "When?"

63
00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:35.051
"When I am dead."

64
00:04:35.071 --> 00:04:37.653
"Then I don't want it!"

65
00:04:38.713 --> 00:04:41.574
Cedric was horrified at the thought of his grandfather's death.

66
00:04:41.594 --> 00:04:44.455
"I wish you'd live forever."

67
00:04:44.475 --> 00:04:49.718
"That's a kind thought," the earl said.

68
00:04:49.738 --> 00:04:57.565
"Nevertheless, someday it will all be yours, and you'll be the Earl of Dorincourt."

69
00:04:59.586 --> 00:05:01.888
Cedric sat very still for a few moments.

70
00:05:03.809 --> 00:05:07.971
He gazed at the broad moors, the green farms, and the pretty village.

71
00:05:09.692 --> 00:05:12.373
Above the trees he could see the towers of the castle.

72
00:05:14.775 --> 00:05:15.735
Then he sighed.

73
00:05:15.755 --> 00:05:19.097
"What are you thinking about?"

74
00:05:19.718 --> 00:05:20.818
the earl asked.

75
00:05:21.899 --> 00:05:27.230
"I was looking at all the houses and thinking about something my mother said yesterday.

76
00:05:29.251 --> 00:05:32.394
She said it's not easy to be an earl.

77
00:05:33.374 --> 00:05:36.516
And that I must learn about the people who live on my land.

78
00:05:37.757 --> 00:05:39.599
That way I'll be able to help them."

79
00:05:43.001 --> 00:05:46.363
Cedric sighed again at the thought of all that responsibility.

80
00:05:46.383 --> 00:05:52.948
"So, Grandpapa, how did you learn about everybody?

81
00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:55.561
The earl flushed.

82
00:05:56.762 --> 00:06:00.785
He only knew which tenants paid their rent and which ones had to be evicted.

83
00:06:01.926 --> 00:06:05.910
He hadn't bothered to learn anything more about the people who lived on his land.

84
00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:11.854
"Reverend Mordaunt tells me what's going on," he finally said.

85
00:06:11.874 --> 00:06:18.340
"When you're an earl, Cedric, make sure you're a better one than I am."

86
00:06:22.108 --> 00:06:25.032
On the ride home, the earl thought about his past.

87
00:06:26.414 --> 00:06:28.477
He wished he'd led a better life.

88
00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:34.926
He would hate for Cedric to know the truth—he was known as "the wicked Earl of
